LAUNCHBILL merge_denied=gateup->down reason=every down row needs all 512 act values, which stage 1 produces across 4 distinct blocks; deleting that boundary buys no launch, it buys a grid-wide barrier. The prob and out stages are the same argument at I->H width. The grouped form is therefore the floor for a launch that is independent of case count, and per-case is exactly 4*n_cases: the two forms are word-identical (gate.py proves that), so nothing here trades blocks-per-launch for launch count.
